        "original_id": "28cd095a-f27c-5c22-9d4e-fb0c74cd9277",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Frederick II (Frederick the Great), Maria Theresa\n- Places: Silesia, Prussia, Austria\n- Events: First Silesian War, Silesian Wars\n- Roles: King of Prussia\n\nFacts:\n- The First Silesian War became the first of three Silesian Wars fought between Prussia under Frederick the Great and Austria under Maria Theresa.\n- Frederick II, also called Frederick the Great, was born on 24 January 1712 and died on 17 August 1786.\n- Frederick II was King of Prussia from 1740 to 1786.\n- Frederick II had the longest reign of any Hohenzollern king.",
